            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.666,
            0.745,
            0.723
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Grade 7, we have learnt that an incandescent lamp glows because its filament is heated by an electric current. Many household appliances, such as electr"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ic room heaters, electric",
              "styles": [
                "underline"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.723,
            0.471,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "stoves, electric kettles, electric irons, water heating immersion rods, and hair dryers (Fig. 4.6) work on the same principle of the heating effect of electric current. All these devices contain a rod or a coil of wire, called a heating element. In some"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.481,
            0.733,
            0.753,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Oh, now I understand why the incandescent torch lamp sometimes used to get warm when we did the activity of making it glow using an electric cell."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
